{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent low bias in rising regimes: when the last 5–10 days show an upswing, add an upward level shift to the whole path (model systematically underprices by ~+1 to +4 €/t, growing with horizon).",
    "Horizon-dependent underestimation: errors increase with lead time; apply a ramping correction (small +0–1 €/t for days 1–5, +2–3 €/t for days 6–15, +3–5 €/t for days 16–30) when trend is positive.",
    "Trend/lag issue: forecasts react too slowly to regime change (breakout from ~62 to high-60s). Use recent momentum: if 10-day return > +3% (or price above 10-day MA by >1 €/t), tilt forecasts upward (increase slope) rather than just shifting level.",
    "Underestimates post-breakout persistence: after a sharp move up, model mean-reverts too quickly. If a 3-day jump > +2 €/t, reduce mean-reversion strength for the next 2–3 weeks (keep prices elevated).",
    "Late-horizon misdirection after strong rallies: the model sometimes projects a pullback (drops into low-60s) while outcomes stay in upper-60s. Impose a floor tied to recent realized levels (e.g., 20-day median or last close minus 1–2 €/t) for days 15–30 during uptrends.",
    "Volatility compression: model paths are too flat vs realized swings in bullish periods. Expand deviations from the recent mean by a factor (e.g., multiply forecast anomalies from 10-day MA by 1.2–1.4) when realized 10-day vol is rising."
  ]
}
